cit ucid="JP-6232838-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6232838</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9046271-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9046271</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1158689A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUMASA HIDENOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHARP KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUMASA, HIDENOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHARP KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUMASA HIDENOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUMASA, HIDENOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A spread-spectrum communication device which has a reduced size, consumes less power and is produced at low cost by suppressing variation of the amplitude of a signal and relaxing the linearity required by an amplifier. A transmission signal is divided into an I-phase component and a Q-phase component. A complex spectrum-spreading unit (301) spreads the spectrum by means of multipliers (304, 305) and adders (302, 303) by using a series pattern in which 1 and -1 alternately appear. The output of the complex spectrum-spreading unit (301) is modulated by multipliers (306, 307) by using a pseudo-random series PN&lt;(k)&gt; (x) assigned to each user. A baseband signal shaped in waveform by roll-off filters (308, 309) is modulated by a carrier modulation unit (316), sent to and amplified by a power amplifier (315), and transmitted from an antenna (317).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un appareil de communication à spectre étalé de petites dimensions, faible consommateur d'électricité et bon marché à fabriquer, se distinguant par une suppression de la variation de l'amplitude d'un signal et le relachement de la linéarité requise par un amplificateur. Un signal de transmission est divisé en une composante phase I et une composante phase Q. Un étaleur de spectres complexes (301) met en oeuvre des multiplicateurs (304, 305) et des additionneurs (302, 303) de façon à étaler le spectre. Il utilise à cet effet des suites faisant alterner 1 et -1. La sortie de l'étaleur de spectres complexes (301) est modulée par les multiplicateurs (306, 307) au moyen des suites pseudo-aléatoires PN&lt;(k)&gt; (x) affectées à chaque utilisateur. Un signal en bande de base mis en forme par des filtres de déroulement (308, 309) est modulé par un modulateur de porteuse, envoyé à et amplifié par un amplificateur de puissance (315) et émis depuis une antenne (317).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://